# __APP_NAME__

A standard HTML + CSS + TypeScript Web Component app, scaffolded by `obix create`.
No `.obix` files, no framework — every component is a real custom element.

```bash
npm install
npm run dev      # http://localhost:5173, live reload
npm run build    # bundle to dist/
npm run check    # tsc --noEmit + accessibility audit
```

## Layout

```
index.html                 app shell (semantic landmarks + <app-counter>)
styles.css                 global styles
src/main.ts                imports each component module
src/components/Counter.ts  a ComponentDef + defineElement()
src/components/Counter.html the template (runtime {marker} bindings)
src/components/Counter.css  scoped styles (shadow DOM)
```

## Adding a component

1. `src/components/Thing.ts` — export a `ComponentDef`, call `defineElement(Thing)`.
2. `src/components/Thing.html` + `Thing.css` — referenced via `new URL("./Thing.html", import.meta.url)`.
3. `import "./components/Thing.ts";` in `src/main.ts`.
4. Use `<app-thing>` in `index.html`.

See [`obix-core`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/obix-core) for the template
binding grammar and the store API.
